WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.067
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 9: Amazing Arts.

2
00:00:03.147 --> 00:00:10.453
In this unit you will explore how art, music, and creative
expression can transform communities and inspire change.

3
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:17.839
You will read about children who turn broken objects into
beautiful instruments, empty walls into colourful murals,

4
00:00:17.919 --> 00:00:20.729
and dusty valleys into thriving green spaces.

5
00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:27.923
Through these stories and activities, you will sharpen
your English skills and discover the power of creativity.

6
00:00:28.003 --> 00:00:33.318
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:33.398 --> 00:00:35.033
By the end of this unit,

8
00:00:35.113 --> 00:00:41.968
you will be able to read and understand a
creative-arts passage and discuss its ideas in English.

9
00:00:42.048 --> 00:00:47.687
You will also use indefinite pronouns
(someone, anyone, everyone, nothing, etc.)

10
00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.332
correctly in sentences.

11
00:00:49.412 --> 00:00:57.553
You will also order multiple adjectives properly before a
noun (opinion → size → age → colour → origin → material).

12
00:00:57.633 --> 00:01:00.199
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:00.279 --> 00:01:06.857
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: deforestation,
landscape, altitude, subtropics, peppermint, turbine.

14
00:01:06.937 --> 00:01:11.588
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:11.668 --> 00:01:15.268
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:15.348 --> 00:01:20.468
The reading sequence includes Introducing
Amazing Arts and The Mural Makers of Mogadishu.

17
00:01:20.548 --> 00:01:21.286
Read actively.

18
00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:25.318
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:25.398 --> 00:01:29.116
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:33.341
The first language focus is Indefinite Pronouns — The Basics.

21
00:01:33.421 --> 00:01:41.375
What it means and why it matters Indefinite pronouns are
words that replace nouns without saying exactly who or what

22
00:01:41.455 --> 00:01:42.345
they refer to.

23
00:01:42.425 --> 00:01:46.916
They let us talk about people,
things, or places in a general way.

24
00:01:46.996 --> 00:01:51.764
For example, instead of naming a
specific person, you can say someone.

25
00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:55.643
Instead of listing every object, you can say everything.

26
00:01:55.723 --> 00:01:59.037
This is very useful in both speaking and writing.

27
00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:06.586
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:06.666 --> 00:02:11.008
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

29
00:02:11.088 --> 00:02:15.180
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.356
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:18.436 --> 00:02:21.656
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:21.736 --> 00:02:23.256
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:23.336 --> 00:02:30.144
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:30.224 --> 00:02:33.483
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:33.563 --> 00:02:41.206
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
